governance/armature_v4_resolutions.md:5:**Status:** Authoritative resolution for architectural and best-practice synthesis questions. Population-specific content decisions (naming, specific axis values, specific mappings) remain subject to revision through PWLE/DPO consultation per §9 of armature v4.
governance/armature_v4_resolutions.md:457:  compliance_status: mandated | recommended | best_practice | unaddressed
governance/armature_v4_resolutions.md:465:2. Also surfaces specifications that have no record for that jurisdiction but are relevant by axis match, marked as "no jurisdiction-specific code reference available — best practice based on international evidence"
governance/audience-priority.md:49:Disabled people use environments. Their lived experience tests whether what gets built actually serves them. The guidebook's claim to evidence-based best practice is empty if it is not legible and accountable to the people whose needs it claims to specify.
governance/audience-priority.md:80:Policymakers shape codes and policy. The guidebook is evidence-grounded best practice that informs rule-making — it is not itself a code and does not aim to become one. Tier 6 codes are the floor; the guidebook specifies the evidence-based aspiration.
governance/audience-priority.md:87:| Rationale | What is the evidence basis for this best-practice value? | Citation chain visible; tier hierarchy applied; gap between code value and evidence-based value made explicit |
governance/co1-operational.md:29:Co-1 is the evidence tier that the Evidence Hierarchy designates as **co-primary with Tier 1 OT-intervention clinical research** for purposes of best-practice claims in this guidebook. The full canonical text is in `governance/mission-and-epistemics.md` §Doctrinal commitments §3 and §Epistemic commitments §Evidence hierarchy. This specification operates within that text; it does not revise it.
governance/co1-operational.md:52:A statement by a single disabled person speaking only for themselves is not Co-1 evidence. It is a personal testimony — meaningful, but not Co-1 in the schematic sense. Co-1 requires methodological grounding: peer review, organizational accountability, or scholarly authorship. The distinction matters because Co-1's epistemic weight in best-practice claims rests on this grounding, not on disability identity alone.
governance/co1-operational.md:66:This is not a courtesy; it is a methodological commitment. A best-practice claim in a domain where Co-1 evidence is available, made without engaging Co-1 evidence, is methodologically incomplete. The evidence hierarchy makes this explicit.
governance/co1-operational.md:149:The voice convention for convergence: "Co-1 and Tier 1 evidence converge on [value]: Tier 1 ([source]) shows [Tier 1 finding]; Co-1 ([source/list]) document [Co-1 finding]; the converged best-practice value is [value]."
governance/co1-operational.md:186:**Audience-priority "disabled people"** (per `governance/audience-priority.md` §Primary audiences) names *who reads the guidebook*. Disabled people are primary audience because the guidebook's claim to evidence-based best practice is empty if it is not legible and accountable to the people whose needs it claims to specify. Their use-patterns are information-finding and representation-checking.
governance/context-map.yaml:167:  - v_best_practice
governance/decision-protocol.md:5:**Doctrinal basis:** `workplan/workplan-co0007-v3.md` §A12 (decision proxy and capture protocol; resolves L-05 model-routing inconsistency) · `workplan/roadmap-2026-04-27.md` §A12 (Pattern: Governance + Code) · `references/project-standards.md` Architecture (Sonnet 4.6 conversational; Opus 4.6 best-practice synthesis) · `references/effort-guide.md` (effort levels 50–150) · CO-0008 Project Instructions update (Opus 4.6 primary)
governance/decision-protocol.md:126:Audit finding L-05 (per `workplan/workplan-co0007-v3.md` §L-05): model-routing notation is inconsistent across phase tables. Some phase tables write "Opus session"; some write "Opus 4.6"; some write "Opus assigned"; some write "best-practice synthesis"; some omit model-routing entirely. Readers cannot reliably tell which model is expected for a given phase.
governance/decision-protocol.md:156:| `opus/150/synth` | Opus-class, effort 150, reasoning modifier = best-practice synthesis |
governance/decision-protocol.md:157:| `fable/150/synth` | Fable-class, effort 150, reasoning modifier = best-practice synthesis |
governance/decision-protocol.md:159:| `sonnet/125/synth` | Sonnet-class, effort 125, reasoning modifier = synthesis (high-end Sonnet load; **not** best-practice synthesis) |
governance/decision-protocol.md:167:Every phase table that records model-routing uses this notation. Old notation forms ("Opus session", "Opus assigned", "best-practice synthesis", etc.) are deprecated — do not use them in new content.
