references/audits/bpc-audit-pass0-2026-05-10.md:413:### F-X3 — "Most cited" vs "best practice" linguistic conflation
references/audits/bpc-audit-pass0-2026-05-10.md:415:The convergence-pattern grep found multiple instances of phrasing like "Aligned on best practice; differ at minimum" (`accessible-circulation-geometry.md` divergent findings table). This phrasing implies code-author agreement is itself the best practice metric. Per the audit thesis, it isn't.
